    "q-112449": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112449",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Due to a quarantine initiated in March $2020$, the number of reservations per night in a hotel decreased by one-quarter each month. By the end of $2020,$ the number of reservations per night decreased to $75\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{9}.$ What does the factor $75$ mean in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot {b}^{t}$, where we have the following:\n\n- $a=75$ represents the initial number of reservations per night.\n\n- $b=\\frac{3}{4}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=9$ is the time, in months, since March $2020.$\n\nSince $a=75,$ this indicates that there were $75$ reservations initially.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-112449-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The number of reservations per night decreased by $75$ each year",
