    "q-85527": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85527",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The daily number of customers to a particular cafe declines according to the expression $500\\cdot (0.83)^{t}$, where $t$ is the number of days since the local news reported that the cafe did not pass a health inspection. \nWhat does the base of the exponential expression $(0.83)$ mean in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1-r)^{t},$ where:\n\n- $a=500$ represents the initial number of customers.\n\n- $1-r=0.83,$ where $r$ is the decay rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time in days since the local news reported that the cafe did not pass a health inspection.\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1-r=0.83\\,⟹\\,r=0.17.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.17$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $17%.$ \n\nSo, the base of the exponential expression $0.83$ means that the number of customers decreases by $17%$ every day.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
